To: CTY, CTS, CCA, CCE, CCB, CCM, CCS
Cc: NOG, UOG, AOG, WOG
Fm: COL


The below and attached is T/S Dwell Time report
of Current average T/S Dwell Time and Long Staying Container list at major T/S ports.

Each team is kindly requested to pay attention on factors that affect CNTR longstaying,
and use this report for prevention of CNTR longstaying at T/S ports and to decrease T/S Dwell time.


* Issues of Longstaying CNTR for or over 7 days at T/S port

1) Space Shortage
    - TLS (GRPIR, 152 BOX, POD: TRIZM, TRMER) : 2 calls made
    - CSS (SGSIN, 142 BOX, POD: BDCGP)
    - FIX (MYPKG, 106 BOX, POD: TWKHH, CNTAO)
    - CKA (KRPUS, 101 BOX, POD: AUBNE)


1. Y2013 Target Ports and KPI

1) Y2013 Target Ports
    - HAMUR: DEHAM, NLRTM, EGPSD, ESALG, ESVLC, GRPIR
    - SHAAS: KRKAN, KRPUS, CNSHA, CNNBO, CNHKG, CNSHU
    - SINWA: AEJEA, AEKLF, MYPKG, SGSIN
    - NYCNA: PAONX

2) Y2013 Target Average Dwell Time KPI: 4.8 Days


2. Current Performance

1) Total Average T/S Dwell Time Performance up to WK45: 4.9 Days (0.1 day over target)

2) Average T/S Dwell Time by RHQ/Ports
    - Performance in RED is which have not achieved KPI Target days.
    - DIFF: Gab between the lastest weekly performance vs. KPI Target.
    - Data source: EDW > Container Operation > Transhipment > T/S PFMC & T/Time

    [cid:5642.jpg@12345678.87654321]
    [cid:BCE2.jpg@12345678.87654321]
    [cid:1F8B.jpg@12345678.87654321]
    [cid:7653.jpg@12345678.87654321]

3. Current Longstaying Container List as of November 21st

   - Long Staying CNTR means CNTRs that are currently staying for or over 7 days at a T/S port.
   - The reasons of longstaying are categorized into 8 types for easier reference.
   - Data source: ALPS > Equipment Management > CNTR Inventory > Inventory Status
                      > Land Inventory > Land Inventory With CNTR List

[cid:16A8.jpg@12345678.87654321]


